WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:38.700
There's a difference between being a drag queen and being transgender. 3, 2, 1...

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:42.180
Girl, I can't twirl over here fast enough.

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:47.669
They are two completely separate things, you know? One's, like, uh...

00:00:48.309 --> 00:00:55.319
artistic expression and one's an actual like gender identity. Yeah, like the easiest way I had someone explain it to me was like:

00:00:55.319 --> 00:00:58.300
"Drag is what you do; trans is who you are."

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:01.500
(YES!) Very well done, well said.

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:02.100
Well, I will say this...

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:02.600
Oh, no.

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:07.500
I know, I know, I know, I know. No, no, no, no, no, I agree with y'all! I agree with y'all!

00:01:07.510 --> 00:01:09.870
I'm clarifying for the people out there because

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:15.569
me in the type of drag that I do-- maybe not with my rainbow hair right now, y'all, but when I have my blond hair

00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:20.309
and my cleavage out and I look like a woman, whether that is a transgender woman or a cisgender woman--

00:01:20.770 --> 00:01:27.300
I get hit up by men in the public who don't know drag, and they do think I'm a woman or they don't understand the difference

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:32.340
even when I tell them. So I do think it is important to know that there are people out there who don't know the difference,

00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:38.819
and, for them, I would just really say: this is an illusion, a pretend, a performance. That is

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:44.489
an identity. And there are people who like to walk the line between both, and that's fine, too.

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:56.500
My family is supportive of my career. 3, 2, 1...

00:01:56.980 --> 00:01:59.489
Um...I will just say it didn't start off that way.

00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:02.250
I started drag a year and some change ago, and

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:09.310
I didn't post anything on Facebook or anything like that until about three months in because I was afraid of it, and then my brother, who

00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:14.819
is the one that I kind of argue with a lot was the first person that actually shared my pictures and was like, "Keep it

00:02:14.819 --> 00:02:18.869
going, I'm proud of you" and everything. And then, from there, all of my family followed suit

00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:22.800
probably because they think I'm going to get rich from it, and they want money, but...

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:29.729
Well, at the age of 17, I got thrown out of my house by my mother on my birthday when they found out I was gay, and

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:36.569
ever since then they haven't supported me up to this day. Yeah, it's very hurtful.

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:40.290
I'm going to change my answer to "somewhat disagree" after hearing your story.

00:02:40.290 --> 00:02:44.279
I remember when I first moved to LA and started getting gigs that like seemed really impressive to me,

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:45.000
I was like, "Dad,

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:50.220
do you know what drag is? I do drag." And he was like, "No, no." And he was like,

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:55.350
"Well, don't tell your mom" because my mom was really sick, and then my mom passed away, and I never told her, and

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:58.320
so that's something that I think about a lot.

00:02:59.350 --> 00:03:04.300
Women can do drag. 3, 2, 1...

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:12.010
You don't have to come here just because we did. Live your truth.

00:03:12.010 --> 00:03:13.350
This is an issue.

00:03:13.350 --> 00:03:16.919
I've always been very divided on, and I have to be very careful with how I say this.

00:03:16.919 --> 00:03:22.050
I do stand divided on what my definition of drag is and where a

00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:28.859
biological, cisgender woman fits into that because obviously, yes, women can do drag because we have a drag king here,

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:35.369
you know, and we have femme Queens and hyper Queens. So yes, they can and they do. Do I personally agree with that?

00:03:35.370 --> 00:03:41.460
I know too many girls who have come up to me and asked me to "teach them drag," and I get them on at a show

00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:45.329
at my home bar, or whatever, and they show up in just, like, their regular club

00:03:45.910 --> 00:03:48.630
makeup and their club outfit. And I'm like girl that is not...

00:03:49.390 --> 00:03:50.800
Well, I can't tell her that's not drag.

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:56.010
I have to jump off of that really quick. My belief is that drag is the art form of gender.

00:03:56.010 --> 00:04:02.309
It is the performing of gender, and we are all negatively impacted by societal expectations of gender.

00:04:02.590 --> 00:04:05.580
How we should or shouldn't sound like, what we should or shouldn't wear,

00:04:05.650 --> 00:04:10.110
what we should or shouldn't be into... And so we all have something to share through drag,

00:04:10.110 --> 00:04:12.749
so to tell anyone that their drag is not valid is

00:04:13.030 --> 00:04:16.559
really frustrating because we all have struggles with gender.

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:23.820
And the thing I will say, as a cis woman, is that like, as women, we are taught our entire life,

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:28.619
you know, to listen to what men tell us about how we're supposed to look. And

00:04:29.140 --> 00:04:35.459
the whole point of drag is to throw all of that in the garbage. I was very feminized as a child, and

00:04:35.980 --> 00:04:37.380
getting really personal here,

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:42.929
but I'm actually a cancer survivor. And I lost my hair and was bald when I was a 7 year old girl, and so

00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:45.730
everyone around me, in the name of

00:04:46.730 --> 00:04:51.699
supporting and loving me--which is beautiful-- tried to make sure to emphasize

00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:56.770
everything that was feminine about me. And, for me, my drag persona and

00:04:57.170 --> 00:05:00.730
discovering drag and doing drag has been all about reclaiming

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:03.500
who I am and my identity.

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:07.370
It's your opinion--and honey, I don't argue with opinions. That's your... live your fantasy.

00:05:07.370 --> 00:05:14.049
But, in my head, that's telling someone, "I'm gonna impersonate you, and I'm gonna live out what I think you are,

00:05:14.050 --> 00:05:16.200
but you can't." To me, that just seems a little off.

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:19.200
And that's what I'm saying. I'm not on the disagree side.

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:24.430
I'm on the "somewhat agree" side because I'm saying, if you're going to do it--and that goes for everybody--

00:05:25.340 --> 00:05:30.300
really do it. Don't be in there, half assing it.

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:31.850
Sometimes people don't know how

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:37.200
to do it. Everyone has a right to look the way they want to.

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:38.400
And I have a right to stand on this line.

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:43.630
No, you're good. Stay over there, but we're still going to disagree with it. You can stay on that side all you want to.

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:51.670
Drag reinforces negative stereotypes about women. 3, 2, 1...

00:05:59.240 --> 00:06:05.920
I chose "strongly disagree" because it said "drag," and I don't think all drag is female impersonation.

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:11.829
I fully agree with that. The only reason I'm here at "somewhat disagree" and not over there is because there are a lot of drag

00:06:12.980 --> 00:06:16.809
standards that reinforce female stereotypes, such as nails,

00:06:17.150 --> 00:06:20.169
lashes, wigs... And there are some amazing, super queer

00:06:20.330 --> 00:06:24.310
performance entertainers that are somewhere in this room that are just amazing and do whatever the fuck they want,

00:06:24.470 --> 00:06:29.000
but there are queens who will go to the club, and they'll read you because they're like, "Girl, you're not wearing nails. Girl,

00:06:29.050 --> 00:06:31.870
your heel is not above five inches." And by

00:06:32.030 --> 00:06:34.239
reinforcing those stereotypes for a drag queen

00:06:34.340 --> 00:06:38.859
impersonating a woman, you're reinforcing those stereotypes on the women that you think should look like that.

00:06:38.860 --> 00:06:44.919
I think a lot of the really unreasonable expectations from drag queens about the nails and the hair and the hips and the that is

00:06:45.200 --> 00:06:52.600
because, suddenly, drag queens are on television. And one of the unfortunate parts about breaking drag to straight people or straight

00:06:52.730 --> 00:06:54.849
audiences is making it, to some degree,

00:06:55.550 --> 00:07:01.639
palatable, and the reason someone like RuPaul shot to fame was because she was stunning. She was beautiful.

00:07:01.639 --> 00:07:02.879
She was a supermodel.

00:07:02.879 --> 00:07:05.359
I think we're definitely seeing the effects of

00:07:05.729 --> 00:07:10.600
stunningly beautiful drag queens on television because now a lot of us are expected to look that way.

00:07:10.600 --> 00:07:12.000
But, in fairness, you could

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:15.139
wear whatever you want. You know, I'm here because I love

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:23.029
the beauty of a woman, the way she looks-- whether if she's skinny, big girls, or any of color.

00:07:23.029 --> 00:07:26.100
It's the beauty; it's the homage that you're giving.

00:07:26.200 --> 00:07:29.778
The problem is not that the Queens and the performers who want to look like a beautiful woman.

00:07:29.810 --> 00:07:35.269
It's the Queens who will judge other Queens for not doing that, for not following these female beauty standards.

00:07:35.969 --> 00:07:39.169
The drag community is diverse and inclusive.

00:07:39.169 --> 00:07:43.520
3, 2, 1...

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:48.080
Dang, y'all.

00:07:49.139 --> 00:07:52.728
I mean... I'm going to have-- Oh, oh, make your shift, make your shift.

00:07:53.909 --> 00:07:54.620
Thank you.

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:57.620
I'm really gonna have to say "somewhat disagree," even from my own

00:07:57.960 --> 00:08:04.279
stance on an opinion question earlier where I didn't believe that necessarily all cisgender women should do drag. Drag is not 100%

00:08:04.349 --> 00:08:10.908
inclusive because I have been told I'm not this enough or I'm not that enough. I had a girl touch my stomach and go,

00:08:10.909 --> 00:08:13.069
"Mm girl, don't you want to wear a girdle?"

00:08:13.069 --> 00:08:18.619
And I said, "No, I don't." So I mean... I can't say that we're totally inclusive.

00:08:18.620 --> 00:08:19.199
I think we're

00:08:19.199 --> 00:08:22.200
going towards that, and we should be, but we're not right now.

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:24.700
And drag, at large, is still such a boys club.

00:08:24.740 --> 00:08:26.250
I know, as a King,

00:08:26.250 --> 00:08:31.849
there's either people don't book Kings at all, or there's like a quota, where they're like,

00:08:31.849 --> 00:08:36.289
"Aww, we're going book a King." And it's like, "No, bitch. I'm

00:08:36.810 --> 00:08:44.359
talented. It is in your best interest to book me. And if you don't book me, I'm going to produce my own show,"

00:08:44.360 --> 00:08:45.500
which is what I did.

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:49.300
Yeah, I feel like there are definitely pockets of inclusivity, and while I do love West Hollywood,

00:08:49.300 --> 00:09:00.000
I will say I didn't start getting booked in West Hollywood until I was on a TV show (Right, right.) 'cause they wouldn't have me there. And it still feels weird sometimes going into that environment.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:01.490
It's weird for for me, too.

00:09:01.490 --> 00:09:04.490
And then that's a place where I also thought: I need to wear nails,

00:09:04.490 --> 00:09:05.870
I need to pad, and all of these things.

00:09:05.870 --> 00:09:10.190
But then I think I felt so much love going to places in downtown, saying,

00:09:10.499 --> 00:09:18.449
"What you're doing is valid," that that's why I'm comfortable enough to walk around in any venue. And it's divided in sections. Absolutely.

00:09:18.449 --> 00:09:23.788
I will not say it's not, but I think there's a spot for everybody in all these areas. I

00:09:24.369 --> 00:09:27.178
I like the way I look outside of drag.

00:09:27.200 --> 00:09:29.600
3, 2, 1...

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:37.220
Bitch, I'm hot out of drag.

00:09:37.620 --> 00:09:39.620
You got to love yourself first,

00:09:39.900 --> 00:09:42.100
then you love the craft.

00:09:42.100 --> 00:09:44.100
I feel very thankful to be happy with the way

00:09:44.120 --> 00:09:48.620
I look outside of drag because I think there are a lot of people that don't. I know a couple of friends who have told

00:09:48.620 --> 00:09:51.890
me that they do drag because it makes them feel more confident with their

00:09:51.990 --> 00:09:55.580
appearances because, outside of drag, they feel ugly, and they feel like a nobody.

00:09:55.580 --> 00:10:01.369
I used to really fucking hate the way I looked. I was a short, skinny kid, and

00:10:01.980 --> 00:10:08.990
I was femme. I was the worst of everything you could possibly be growing up Catholic and Mexican in the South,

00:10:08.990 --> 00:10:10.990
you know? Through drag, I

00:10:11.010 --> 00:10:16.700
was able to find the things I loved about myself and kind of feed that until I got to a point where I

00:10:17.190 --> 00:10:20.179
really don't give a shit anymore. I love the way I look. I fucking love it.

00:10:20.180 --> 00:10:22.940
I don't know if I would have gotten there without the drag.

00:10:22.940 --> 00:10:28.760
I mean, I love the way I look out of drag. I'm a big guy, which is harder to be a gay man

00:10:28.770 --> 00:10:34.429
who is larger. I can go to West Hollywood and drag and sit VIP at Pomp or Sir.

00:10:34.430 --> 00:10:40.820
If I go as a boy, I got to check my ID, pay maybe double the cover, you know?

00:10:40.820 --> 00:10:44.030
No one's gonna buy me a drink. I got to buy the doorman a drink. It's like that.

00:10:44.460 --> 00:10:51.200
So I love myself out of drag. I just need y'all to love me up out a drag. You can find me. Hello! Thank you!

00:10:51.330 --> 00:10:56.960
I've seen all of you outside of drag. It's a very distinct look. And I like y'all outside of drag!

00:10:56.960 --> 00:11:04.000
I don't know if that counts for anything 'cause it's your opinion, but, listen, I live for y'all outside of drag. I'm glad for y'all to live for yourselves.

00:11:06.500 --> 00:11:07.400
Thank you so much.

00:11:09.360 --> 00:11:14.720
Hey, guys, thank you so much for watching this episode. Tell us your favorite moment from this video.

00:11:14.760 --> 00:11:17.760
Who do you relate to the most? And what

00:11:18.060 --> 00:11:22.070
expectations were shattered, and what judgements were thrown out the window? Follow us on Instagram.

00:11:22.070 --> 00:11:25.300
We have some more content for you there, and thank you as always for

00:11:25.950 --> 00:11:30.619
letting us make things that explore the spectrum of humanity in all types of ways. We'll see you next time.

00:11:30.619 --> 00:11:32.619
Bye! (Bye.)

